# Building a replacement HEVC decoder module

`hevc-decoder.wasm` is FFmpeg's libavcodec HEVC decoder and libavutil (LGPL 2.1
or later, `FFmpeg-LGPL-2.1.txt`), linked as one side module. The program that
loads it provides the Emscripten and musl runtime (`Emscripten-LICENSE.txt`,
`musl-COPYRIGHT.txt`). To replace the FFmpeg part with a build of your own:

1. Take the FFmpeg @FFMPEG_VERSION@ source (`@FFMPEG_URL@`, SHA-256
   `@FFMPEG_SHA256@`), or your own FFmpeg source.
2. Install Emscripten @EMSCRIPTEN_VERSION@.
3. Configure and build the two libraries:

   ```sh
   emconfigure ./configure @CONFIGURE_FLAGS@
   emmake make libavutil/libavutil.a libavcodec/libavcodec.a
   ```

4. Link the two libraries into one side module with `emcc`, as
   `scripts/build.sh` does (`-sSIDE_MODULE=2`, exporting the functions listed in
   `scripts/flags.sh`). A program links the module by naming it on its `emcc`
   command line with `-sMAIN_MODULE=2` (see `scripts/check.sh`).

`scripts/build.sh` in the repository performs all of these steps.
